{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41549 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Gelsemicine is implicated in the biological activity of HCC1937 through a series of target relationships, with SNU-387 acting as a common intermediary. The evidence suggests that Gelsemicine targets SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds, in turn, have HCC1937 as their target. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Gelsemicine may influence HCC1937 through the activation of downstream targets that are involved in cellular processes affecting the tumor cell line. The evidence supports a role for Gelsemicine in modulating the activity of these compounds, which may contribute to its effect on HCC1937. The relationship is supported by a consistent pattern of target interactions, suggesting a plausible biological pathway that connects Gelsemicine to HCC1937 through SNU-387.",
